From 144ce34e846b3f732bdb003f99b1f9455425416f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Eskil Abrahamsen Blomfeldt <eskil.abrahamsen-blomfeldt@qt.io>
Date: Fri, 31 Oct 2025 09:08:51 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Rich text: Limit size of text object

When we draw a text object, we need to store this in RAM
since the QTextObjectInterface is QPainter-based. This
could lead to over-allocation if the text object size
was set to be very large. We use the existing image IO
infrastructure for making sure allocations are within
reasonable (and configurable) limits.

Downstream adaptation (Qt 5 backport):
Qt 5 lacks QImageIOHandler::allocateImage() and the image reader allocation
limit API. Provide local equivalents using Qt 5's image size calculations.
The limit defaults to 256 MiB and can be overridden for text objects with
QT_IMAGEIO_MAXALLOC; zero disables the limit. Return on allocation failure to
avoid passing a null image to the Qt 5 scene graph. Adapt the test to use
Qt 5's qWaitForItemPolished().

Pick-to: 5.15 6.5 6.8 6.10
Task-number: QTBUG-141515
Change-Id: Ieae06a9e92a7bd078d22ab2314889201c2049122
Reviewed-by: Eirik Aavitsland <eirik.aavitsland@qt.io>
